    "created_at": "2015-08-28T13:12:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-08-28T13:12:57Z",
    "body": "(Thanks for reporting! You got it right.)\n\nI can't find the prohibition on newlines that you mention in the textarea section... Could you quote the confusing text? In fact I see the opposite:\n\n>  All U+000D CARRIAGE RETURN U+000A LINE FEED character pairs (CRLF) in the hint, as well as all other U+000D CARRIAGE RETURN (CR) and U+000A LINE FEED (LF) characters in the hint, must be treated as line breaks when rendering the hint.\n\nNote that the textarea placeholder attribute is different from the input placeholder attribute, so if you are looking at the input section, that's not the right place to go.\n\n> In addition, the version at html.spec.whatwg.org directly links from the section on textarea to the misleading section on placeholder.\n\nHmm. When I click that link, then click the \"placeholder\" link, I get to the textarea placeholder attribute section, which as mentioned above doesn't have a prohibition and in fact has the opposite.\n\nLet me know what I'm missing...\n",
