    "created_at": "2015-08-28T14:36:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-08-28T14:36:36Z",
    "body": "Hmm. There really is a clear distinction between inputs and textareas, though. They are processed differently in a substantial number of ways. I don't think we want to start conflating them. You may consider input type=\"text\" and textarea conceptually closer than input type=\"text\" and input type=\"radio\", but in terms of parsing rules, browser implementation internals, and spec text, the opposite is true. inputs have certain attributes and properties; textareas don't. input's placeholder attribute is simply different from textarea's placeholder, similar to link's sizes vs. img's sizes.\n\nThe table of contents issue is interesting, but really it's just a reflection of the fact that we don't have a section for every attribute. The \"Common input element attributes\" sections and \"Attributes common to form controls\" are exceptions. But if you're looking for e.g. option's disabled attribute you'll also be disappointed that it doesn't show up in the TOC>\n\nIssues with developers.whatwg.org's search are another thing too... that hasn't been updated in a long time, and perhaps needs its own repo. It's kind of a separate project, although for now there's nothing wrong with reporting bugs on it here. Maybe that's the action item, is to make their search more aware?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
